Chronicle — Clean Continuation Prompt (Claude‑Ready)
Paste this at the start of a new Claude Code session.

Project Overview
Chronicle — a personal diary + calendar PWA.
Vanilla JS (ES modules), HTML5, CSS3. No framework, no build step.
Mobile‑first (Android primary), desktop supported.

Location: s:\Coding\Diary Calendar\

File Structure
Code
index.html
js/
  app.js
  calendar.js
  diary.js
  events.js
  gestures.js
  holidays.js
  ical.js
  notifications.js
  sync.js
  themes.js
  themeEditor.js
  undo.js
css/
  base.css
  ribbon.css
  week-view.css
  day-card.css
  expanded-day.css
  modals.css
  agenda.css
  themes.css
  responsive.css
assets/
  icons.svg
Theme System (Required Context)
Chronicle has a full UI + event theme engine.
Stored in data.settings:

js
{
  uiTheme: 'default',
  uiThemeCustomVars: { light: {...}, dark: {...} },
  customUIThemes: [ { id, name, swatch, light, dark } ],
  eventThemeOverrides: {},
  customEventThemes: []
}
Built‑in UI Themes
Default, Warm, Forest, Slate, Hi‑Contrast.
Each has 12 CSS vars for light/dark.

Built‑in Event Themes
Birthday, Work, Holiday, Personal, Appointment.

CSS Injection
applyUITheme(settings) → injects UI theme CSS

injectEventThemeCSS(settings) → injects event theme CSS
Both must always be called together.

Theme Editor
Bottom sheet with 3 tabs: Presets, UI Colours, Events.
HSV picker, live preview, custom theme saving, export/import.

Key Patterns & Conventions
Plain ES modules, no build step

State lives in app.js

Save = saveData() → localStorage

Modals use history API (pushState / popstate)

Event/todo titles stored as HTML

Use esc() when inserting user content

Touch‑first interactions

Format toolbar is a singleton

refreshVisibleWeekCards() for event-strip updates

Holiday data not stored as events

No emojis in UI text

CSS variables everywhere

